.\" Manpage for letux-esp-serial-flasher
.\" Contact letux-kernel@openphoenux.org to correct errors or typos.
.TH man 1 "11 June 2026" "1.0" "letux-esp-serial-flasher man page"
.SH NAME
letux-esp-serial-flasher \- tool to flash embedded ESP32-C6-WROOM-1 with esp-host-ng firmware in-circuit for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
/usr/local/bin/mipsel-linux-gnu/letux-esp-serial-flasher [-bbaud] [-d/dev/ttyS#] [-ffirmware] [-w] [-p0-2]
.SH DESCRIPTION
letux-esp-serial-flasher is a tool to flash the ESP32C6 of the LX16 and derived boards.
.SH OPTIONS
The letux-esp-serial-flasher takes some options.
-b### set baud rate [115200]
-d### set serial device [/dev/ttyS1]
-w flash 'Hello World' example instead of the firmware
-f### set firmware directory [/lib/firmware/espressif/esp32-c6-wroom-1]
-p### set power [0=off 1=on 2=boot]
.SH FILES
Firmware is stored in /usr/local/lib/firmware/espressif/esp32-c6-wroom-1 (unless overwritten by -f)
Access to device tree is required /proc/device-tree/...
A serial port /dev/ttyS1 (unless overwritten by -d) to the UART pins
.SH HARDWARE
requires sdio connection to device plus UART and control GPIOs.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/espressif/esp-serial-flasher/tree/master/examples/raspberry_example
.SH BUGS
No known bugs.
.SH AUTHOR
H. Nikolaus Schaller (hns@goldelico.com)
